{
  "id": "reactive-attachment-disorder",
  "term": "reactive attachment disorder",
  "definition": "Reactive attachment disorder is a diagnosis describing severe, developmentally inappropriate problems in how a young child relates socially, beginning before age 5 and linked to grossly pathological caregiving. It may involve a persistent failure to start or respond to social interaction in an age-appropriate way, or unusually indiscriminate sociability with diffuse attachments.",
